  "id": "compensatory-tracking",
  "term": "compensatory tracking",
  "definition": "Compensatory tracking is a closed-loop task used to study human control performance by having a person use feedback information to guide actions so their output follows a reference trajectory. It serves as a standard way to test how features of the feedback affect tracking performance.",
